vote, so you can't simply punch someone out of their BP, and it asks that you admonish them publicly... if you had a chance to fail on top of all of that, it would be worthless in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T13:57:13-08:00","id":827763,"title":"","content":"Eh, its a curse that scales depending on how much support it gets, and doesn't actually remove a good chunk of the opponent's power. I think its fine as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T20:46:14-08:00","id":827960,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's incredibly powerful and incredibly hard to make work.<br /> Anyway, the target can <i>already</i> resist it - they can tamper (or &quot;aggressively dismantle&quot;) all of your set-up work. This isn't about &quot;roll to cripple someone;&quot; this Merit is a story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T03:00:06-08:00","id":828103,"title":"","content":"It's not hard to make work. It's the Carthian Lynch Mob power. It does allow a sizeable portion of Carthians to quickly tear down the Dragon's 6 BP champion frenzy master and destroy them. In the hands of an ST character, it's either a plot device (which in that case they don't NEED to meet the criteria) or when used arbitrarily against PCs or by other PCs in a PVP setting, a shitty way to invalidate a player's investiture in Blood Potency. As it's written right now, if the Carthian Movement is nothing more than a coterie of three vampires, they can literally name one vampire from within as their leader (5 status) and run around assassinating the neonate childer of some random elder or ancillae who pissed them off. There are NO criteria whatsoever for requiring a quora to vote, no guidelines as to what constitutes a valid admonishment or if any outright lie or tangential target works, and no risk of loss for a failed vote. (Like backfiring and affecting the initiator or loss of status due to the transparent pettiness for the reasons of the vote.) And if that's the scenario that's closer to the OP's issue with the power, then I would suggest either installing a quora and admonishment guidelines or saying the blood potency loss only applies for a number of nights equal to the number of vampires who vote in favor of admonishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T04:25:29-08:00","id":828124,"title":"","content":"I am fairly certain the Merit assumes two things: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The Carthian Movement is not a hive mind, quite the opposite in fact (despite what certain strains of it might aspire to)</li> <li>The political situation in most domains is more complicated than Us vs. Them along covenant lines</li> </ol><br /> If these two things are true, I have to side with the users saying that it is hard to make work. You have to have a lot of Carthians agreeing on its use, this includes Carthians who might have positive dealings with the target, Carthians who might be opposed to the admonisher and Carthians who want to keep a relative amount of peace in the domain.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, in a domain in which the Carthians are not the dominant power, I think the target can make a very valid case that they are, in fact, being attacked by the Carthian enacting this and therefore have a casus belli to reply with equal force.<br /> <br /> If a Carthian character can truly mobilise the entire Movement of a city to use the Merit to its full effect than either they are a superb politician and manipulator who put it all into this or the target really fucking had it coming. Both are perfectly fine by me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T04:42:22-08:00","id":828133,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, its also assuming that, once you make the Mandate, it will actually affect their power base in some way. An Invictus retainer-master, with lots of people Oathed to him, is content to sit back and let his servants and knights deal with any threat. A Lancea et Sanctum or Circle of the Crone sorcerer is still going to have the full breadth of their magical abilities and the respect of their peers. <br /> <br /> Good luck with that. Just because you can use it doesn't mean you should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}